    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • 2027 Hyundai Bayon Finally Looks More Like a Box and Less Like an Egg\n2027 Ineos Grenadier Helmsman Launches New Special Edition Series Inspired by 'The Elements'\n6 photos\nPhoto: Ineos Automotive\nThe Ineos Grenadier off-road vehicle is preparing to enter the 2027 model year with a new special edition dubbed Helmsman in tow. More will come in the near future, all inspired by “the elements.”\nIneos Automotive Ltd is a British manufacturer of off-road vehicles based in London, established in 2016 after Sir Jim Ratcliffe, the chairman of the multinational chemicals company Ineos, failed to purchase the rights to build the classic Defender from Land Rover.\nHis version is a similar vehicle, named after the guy’s favorite pub, The Grenadier, in Belgravia, London, and has been produced since 2022 in Hambach, France, with a steel ladder chassis, beam axles, boxy styling, and BMW powertrains, including the B57 turbo diesel and B58 turbo inline-six plus the classic ZF eight-speed automatic transmission.\nOver the years, the Ineos Grenadier has risen in popularity, and the company can easily name it a successful first-time project. More so, Ineos has been expanding the reach of the Grenadier in recent months with defense bids – they went into competition for the British Ministry of Defence’s Light Mobility Vehicle program back in September and also announced that the Italian Army and the Austrian government awarded them substantial orders and contracts for their enhanced protection versions of the Grenadier.\nOf course, Ineos doesn’t forget that retail clients are very important, and inspired by one of the most important elements in nature, the tides, has introduced the Grenadier Helmsman model for the 2027 model year as the launch version of a new series of special editions. It “charts the course for a new line of special editions inspired by the elements Grenadier was designed to tackle” and will be available in both Station Wagon and Quartermaster versions.\nObviously aimed at fans with a passion for navigation, the Helmsman “reflects a nautical lifestyle and builds on the appeal of the standard Grenadier.” The new limited series has popular design elements taken from previous special editions and mixes them with a deep blue paint originally developed by Arcane Works.\nThe new 2027 Ineos Grenadier Helmsman also has exclusive badges, a Dark Exterior Pack featuring a black grille, dark skid plates, and all-new matte black roof rails, plus 17-inch diamond-cut alloy wheels. It also adds privacy glass, heated leather seats, carpet floor mats mixed with heavy-duty wash-down rubber flooring, locking wheel nuts, and the rear access ladder or load bay tub.\nThere are also features from the Smooth Pack like ambient lighting, front parking sensors, and auxiliary electrical points. In addition to the blue, there is also a Whiteout Blue metallic exterior paint option, also previously exclusive to Arcane Works models. The standard paints are Eldoret Blue and Scottish White, with optional contrast roofs in Inky Black or Scottish White. Inside, Helmsman introduces oyster-colored inserts for the black leather seats.\nPricing kicks off at £70,995 for the new 2027 Ineos Grenadier Helmsman, which is about $94k at the current exchange rate, but you need to hurry because it “will have a limited production window ahead of the next elements-inspired special edition.”\nBuilt to work hard and play even harder, the Grenadier is in its element when recovering a boat or transporting kayaks to the coast. With this in mind, we have combined popular design features from previous limited editions with new oceanic hues to deliver the ideal 4X4 for watersports enthusiasts and seafarers. After three quarters of double-digit growth, it’s clear that our model line-up evolution is focused on bringing new customers to the brand who share our spirit of adventure,” explains Sagree Sardien, Global Sales Director at Ineos Grenadier.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2027 Ineos Grenadier Helmsman ineos grenadier ineos Grenadier Special Edition 2027MY pricing UK\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Durable Force Is the Bad Boy Face of the 2027 Kawasaki KLR650 Adventure Bike",
